Description: Force --disable-bootstrap to avoid RTL SSA ICE during stage2
 The stage1 gcc binary compiled from this source has a latent bug in its
 RTL SSA pass (rtl_ssa::sort_accesses) that causes a reproducible ICE
 when recompiling fs_path.cc during stage2 of the 3-stage bootstrap on
 virtualized amd64 hosts. Forcing with_bootstrap := off limits the build
 to a single-stage compilation by the system gcc, which does not exhibit
 the bug, while still producing a fully functional gcc-12 toolchain.
 Patches debian/rules.defs directly (a debian/ file, no quilt needed).
Author: Harkirat S Virk <harkiratsvirk@gmail.com>
Origin: local
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-05-04
---
This patch header follows DEP-3: http://dep.debian.net/deps/dep3/
--- a/debian/rules.defs
+++ b/debian/rules.defs
@@ -363,6 +363,9 @@
 ifneq ($(findstring nostrap, $(DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS)),)
   with_bootstrap := off
 endif

+# Athena Linux: single-stage build to avoid stage2 RTL SSA ICE on virt hosts
+with_bootstrap := off
+
 ifneq ($(findstring nolto, $(DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS)),)
   with_lto_build :=
